{{!-- The Season tab, filed by WHEN a thing is done.

      It used to run wheel → the full four-step turn panel → moments → the other seasons, with the
      improvement board under all of it. So the largest, loudest element was the one act performed
      ONCE a season, and everything used THROUGHOUT one sat below it, below the fold.

      The cut is when, not what: the turn is a control, shut until the table is ready to turn, and
      "During <season>" is the working surface — the gain in force, what the steading's buildings owe
      this season, and the moments within it. The board follows, second now rather than fifth.

      Params: seasons (SeasonsSnapshot). --}}
<div class="steading-seasons">

	{{> "stonetop.steading-season-wheel" seasons=seasons}}

	{{> "stonetop.steading-season-turn" seasons=seasons}}

	{{!-- Everything the season you are IN is owed, in one place. Each of these was previously a step
	      of the turn panel or a section under it, which put what autumn owes inside the act of
	      leaving autumn for winter. --}}
	<section class="steading-during steading-block">

		{{> "stonetop.section-heading"
		    title=(localize "stonetop.steading.seasons.during"
		           season=(localize seasons.turnover.season.labelKey))}}

		{{!-- What this season handed the table on the way in, in force until the wheel turns again.
		      Picked at the roll — "on a 10+, pick 2 seasonal gains" — but what you picked is a rule
		      read all season ("take +1 to Pull Together this season"), so it stays out here rather
		      than behind the turn's disclosure.

		      Which list, and how many, is this season's own move's business: spring and autumn offer
		      one gain, summer two, and winter offers no gains at all — it takes. The tab used to hand
		      every season the same six gains at "pick 1". --}}
		{{#if seasons.pick}}
			<div class="steading-during-gain">
				<h4 class="steading-during-label">
					{{localize seasons.pick.labelKey count=seasons.pick.count}}
				</h4>
				{{#with seasons.pick.group}}{{> "stonetop.choice-group" cgContext="steading"}}{{/with}}
			</div>
		{{/if}}

		{{!-- Headed by the TRIGGER, in the book's own terms — "When winter comes" — so that no row
		      under it has to say when it fires. What the heading said before was
		      "Because of what Stonetop has built", a noun that names the SOURCE of every row while
		      each row went on to restate its own trigger: the half that differed between rows was
		      buried behind a clause they all shared. --}}
		<div class="steading-during-owed">
			<h4 class="steading-during-label">
				{{localize "stonetop.steading.seasons.whenComes"
				           season=(localize seasons.turnover.season.labelKey)}}
			</h4>
			{{> "stonetop.steading-turnover" turnover=seasons.turnover}}
		</div>

		{{!-- The results that bend a STEP of the season rather than adding to it, gathered under the
		      step. Separate from the block above because they are a different kind of thing: not what
		      the season pays out, but how the season's own arithmetic works for this steading. --}}
		{{> "stonetop.steading-adjustments" statement=seasons.turnover.statement}}

		{{!-- The named points WITHIN the season that something built fires at — the harvest coming in,
		      the hunt being led. The sheet cannot know when those happen, so each is an offer the
		      table takes up rather than a schedule. Only moments something actually fires at appear. --}}
		{{#if seasons.turnover.hasMoments}}
			{{> "stonetop.steading-moments" turnover=seasons.turnover momentSteps=seasons.momentSteps}}
		{{/if}}

	</section>

</div>
